WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.640
At least 10 people died when two high-speed trains collided in Central Spain, closing the Madrid

00:00:04.640 --> 00:00:11.340
Seville line. This is Omni View, episode 219. Canada's trade pact with the United Arab Emirates,

00:00:11.780 --> 00:00:16.900
Hong Kong's export jump, a Brazilian Senators' departure, then understanding the issue.

00:00:17.540 --> 00:00:23.140
Near Moira and Orgas in Toledo Province, a rent-faced service and an IRIO service were both heading

00:00:23.140 --> 00:00:28.520
from Madrid towards Seville when they met in a rear-end collision just after 9 a.m. local time.

00:00:28.520 --> 00:00:32.340
Two iron wagons derailed and fell down an embankment.

00:00:32.840 --> 00:00:37.800
Deutsche Vela reports, and Spanish authorities said the death toll could still rise. France

00:00:37.800 --> 00:00:43.400
24 walks through the emergency timeline. Officials in Castilla, La Mancha called the situation

00:00:43.400 --> 00:00:48.720
serious and sent multiple fire crews, three helicopters, and two mobile intensive care

00:00:48.720 --> 00:00:54.420
units. Prime Minister Pedro Sanchez said he was shocked by the serious accident. He directed

00:00:54.420 --> 00:00:58.860
Emergency services to coordinate with all involved administrations to assist victims

00:00:58.860 --> 00:00:59.960
and ensure safety.

00:01:00.540 --> 00:01:05.000
Witnesses describe numerous injuries, and the exact number of people hurt is still being

00:01:05.000 --> 00:01:05.480
determined.

00:01:06.240 --> 00:01:10.600
Emergency services ask the mayor of Urda to prepare a sports hall to accommodate the

00:01:10.600 --> 00:01:10.860
injured.

00:01:11.460 --> 00:01:16.220
This is the second major rail incident in Spain this year, after a January crash that

00:01:16.220 --> 00:01:17.460
killed 45 people.

00:01:18.000 --> 00:01:19.740
The cause remains under investigation.

00:01:20.900 --> 00:01:22.960
Investigators will examine how the collision happened.

00:01:22.960 --> 00:01:28.545
Prime Minister Mark Carney's government signed a comprehensive economic partnership agreement

00:01:28.545 --> 00:01:34.125
with the United Arab Emirates, a deal al-Jazeera places an Ottawa's push toward markets beyond

00:01:34.125 --> 00:01:35.065
the United States.

00:01:35.505 --> 00:01:40.165
The pact is designed to cut tariffs on more than 99 percent of current Canadian exports

00:01:40.165 --> 00:01:43.285
to the UAE and to reduce red tape for businesses.

00:01:43.905 --> 00:01:46.745
It is expected to enter into force in 2027.

00:01:47.485 --> 00:01:53.245
Covered sectors include agriculture, industrial machinery, aerospace, power generation equipment

00:01:53.245 --> 00:01:54.965
and environmental services.

00:01:55.385 --> 00:01:57.785
Preliminary agreements on energy, diplomatic,

00:01:58.085 --> 00:02:00.865
and defense cooperation were signed at the same ceremony.

00:02:01.505 --> 00:02:04.885
Karni has sought to expand non-US trade over the next decade

00:02:04.885 --> 00:02:06.785
amid tensions with the United States.

00:02:07.245 --> 00:02:09.045
The UAE's foreign trade minister,

00:02:09.565 --> 00:02:11.205
Thani Bin Ahmed Al-Zayudi,

00:02:11.745 --> 00:02:13.905
highlighted potential for private sector growth

00:02:13.905 --> 00:02:16.905
in logistics, communications, advanced technology,

00:02:17.125 --> 00:02:17.825
and manufacturing.

00:02:18.525 --> 00:02:21.105
The deal aims to create a more predictable environment

00:02:21.105 --> 00:02:22.345
for trade and investment.

00:02:22.345 --> 00:02:30.025
It also targets non-tariff barriers in industrial, agricultural, forest, fish and seafood and engineering sectors.

00:02:31.102 --> 00:02:37.782
Exports from Hong Kong rose 64.9% year-on-year in September, according to the South China Morning Post.

00:02:38.362 --> 00:02:42.082
The total reached 762.6 billion Hong Kong dollars.

00:02:42.622 --> 00:02:45.002
That was the highest growth in more than 40 years.

00:02:45.972 --> 00:02:49.352
The increase continued a streak of 20 consecutive months of expansion.

00:02:49.352 --> 00:02:54.192
